Vendored files and what was changed in each:

  lib_krea2_area/schedule.py   from area/schedule.py; unchanged apart from a header line
                               naming the source.
  lib_krea2_area/tiling.py     from area/tiling.py; unchanged apart from a header line
                               naming the source.
  lib_krea2_area/bridge.py     from area/bridge.py; unchanged apart from a header line
                               naming the source.
  lib_krea2_area/attention.py  from area/attention.py; header line added; the import of
                               diffusers' dispatch_attention_fn removed; windowed_attention
                               takes an attention callable (`attn`, [B, L, H, D] in and out)
                               in place of its `backend` argument, defaulting to a new
                               sdpa_attention helper (PyTorch scaled_dot_product_attention);
                               its docstring notes that the bridge-ranking keys may carry
                               fewer heads than the attention keys.

Everything else in this repository (the Krea 2 adapter, the Forge Neo script, the tests
and the documentation) is original to this project and is, in the sense of the Apache
License, a Derivative Work of the AReA sample code where it adapts upstream's FLUX.1
backbone adapter (area/backbones/flux.py and area/backbones/base.py) to Krea 2.
